# CODEOWNERS — automatic review routing for pull requests.
#
# GitHub reads this file and requests a review from the listed owner(s)
# whenever a PR touches a matching path. Last matching pattern wins, so
# put the broad rule (*) first and the specific ones after it.
#
# To make reviews mandatory (merge blocked until an owner approves),
# enable "Require review from Code Owners" in Settings → Branches →
# branch protection rules. Without it, this file only pings reviewers.
#
# Syntax:
#   <path pattern>   @user [@user2 ...] [@org/team]
#   *                matches every file
#   docs/            matches everything under docs/
#   *.ts             matches every TypeScript file
#   # comment        ignored by GitHub

# Default owner: everything not matched below.
*                      @SirEriTheRed

# CI, workflows and community health files.
.github/               @SirEriTheRed

# Source code and its tests.
src/                   @SirEriTheRed
tests/                 @SirEriTheRed

# Hand-written documentation (generated docs/api/ needs no review).
docs/                  @SirEriTheRed

# Release-critical files: a bad merge here ships a bad release.
package.json           @SirEriTheRed
package-lock.json      @SirEriTheRed
.releaserc.json        @SirEriTheRed
